     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled metformin dose. The usual limits are:\n\n- **Immediate-release:** up to 2,550 mg/day, given as 850 mg three times daily with meals. Single doses are typically no more than 1,000 mg.\n- **Extended-release:** up to 2,000 to 2,500 mg/day.\n\nA dose this high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis. This is true even with normal renal and hepatic function.\n\nPossible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max for IR).\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose**, such as a typical starting dose of 500 mg twice daily or 850 mg once daily, titrated up.\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm that 1700 mg three times daily is what you meant. If you confirm it, I'll enter it with a note that it exceeds the maximum dose. I'll enter the order as soon as I hear from you."
      }
     ],
